# Connect to your PostgreSQL server

Your PostgreSQL instance is running and reachable on the address below.

- **Host:** `{{ .Host }}`
- **Port:** `{{ .Port }}`
- **Superuser:** `{{ .Username }}`

## psql

```bash
psql "host={{ .Host }} port={{ .Port }} user={{ .Username }} dbname=postgres"
```

or with a connection URL (you will be prompted for the password):

```bash
psql "postgresql://{{ .Username }}@{{ .Host }}:{{ .Port }}/postgres"
```

## Password

The superuser password is **not shown here and is never stored by Proxcloud**.
It was displayed **once**, at creation time, in the provisioning response — save
it in your password manager now. If you did not capture it, connect over SSH and
reset it in-guest:

```bash
sudo -u postgres psql -c "ALTER ROLE {{ .Username }} WITH PASSWORD 'a-new-strong-password';"
```

## Security note

This server accepts password (scram-sha-256) connections from the network so you
can reach it remotely. Restrict access with the guest firewall or your LAN before
putting real data on it — see the service's exposed ports ({{ .Port }}/tcp).
